The standard benchmark does:
1. offsetMomentum: subtract total momentum / SOLAR_MASS from Sun's velocity to make system momentum zero.
2. Print initial energy.
3. advance N steps: for each pair (i, j), compute distance, update velocities; then update positions.
4. Print final energy.

The standard advance:

```c
void advance(int nbodies, double *vx, ...) {
  for (i=0; i<nbodies; i++) {
    Body &bi = bodies[i];
    for (j=i+1; j<nbodies; j++) {
      Body &bj = bodies[j];
      double dx = bi.x - bj.x;
      ...
      double d2 = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz;
      double mag = dt / (d2 * sqrt(d2));
      bi.vx -= dx * bj.mass * mag;
      ...
      bj.vx += dx * bi.mass * mag;
      ...
    }
  }
  for (i=0; i<nbodies; i++) {
    Body &b = bodies[i];
    b.x += dt * b.vx;
    ...
  }
}
```

