// reverse-complement — reads FASTA DNA from stdin, writes the reverse
// complement of every sequence to stdout, preserving each header line
// verbatim and the original line wrapping (sequence lines are emitted in
// reverse order, each line reversed and complemented — the canonical FASTA
// reverse-complement layout).

